#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:2
msgid "Haptic feedback protocol"
msgstr "触觉反馈协议"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:6
msgid ""
"Some input devices can tap back at the user: the trackpads of Apple laptops and the Magic "
"Trackpad, pens such as the Surface Slim Pen 2 and the Apple Pencil Pro, and dials such as the "
"Surface Dial. Applications use that for the moment a dragged object snaps into alignment, for the"
" end of a gesture, for a pen touching down, and on a pen for the drag of a pencil or a brush over"
" paper. The haptic feedback protocol lets a terminal program ask for the same. It is small on "
"purpose: a program asks what can be played, then asks for a tap, or starts and stops the feel of "
"a tool. A terminal without the hardware, or without the protocol, does nothing."
msgstr ""
"某些输入设备可以向用户回馈轻触感：Apple 笔记本触控板和 Magic Trackpad，Surface Slim Pen 2、Apple Pencil Pro 等笔，以及 Surface "
"Dial "
"等旋钮。应用可用它表示拖动物体吸附对齐、手势结束、笔落下，或在笔上模拟铅笔／画笔划过纸面的阻力。触觉反馈协议让终端程序请求同类反馈。协议刻意保持简洁：先查询可播放内容，再请求轻触，或开始／停止工具质感。没有硬件或不支持协议的终端不执行操作。"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:17
msgid "Framing"
msgstr "消息封装"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:19
msgid "Frames are ``OSC 777`` with the ``haptic`` selector::"
msgstr "帧使用带有 ``haptic`` 选择器的 ``OSC 777``：::"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:23
msgid ""
"They follow the rules every OSC 777 extension shares, which :doc:`extension-framing` gives: the "
"syntax of the fields, which frames are rejected and the units. ``v``, the protocol version, is "
"``1``, and ``op`` is one of ``query``, ``cap``, ``play``, ``start`` and ``stop``. A request whose"
" ``op`` is not one of these, or with a value that is not one of those defined for its key, is "
"ignored as a whole as well. The terminal sends only replies, which are never merged or dropped."
msgstr ""
"帧遵循 :doc:`extension-framing` 规定的 OSC 777 共用规则：字段语法、拒绝哪些帧，以及单位。协议版本 ``v`` 为 ``1``，``op`` 为 "
"``query``、``cap``、``play``、``start`` 或 ``stop``。``op`` "
"不在其中，或某个键的值不是已定义值时，也会忽略整条请求。终端仅发送回复，回复绝不合并或丢弃。"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:31
msgid ""
"Feedback is played on a *target*, named by the ``target`` field of the requests below: "
"``trackpad``, which is what is meant when the field is absent, ``pen``, the pen in use on a "
"tablet or a screen, or ``dial``. A request for a target the terminal cannot play on is dropped."
msgstr ""
"反馈在 *目标* 上播放，由请求中的 ``target`` 指定：``trackpad``（省略字段时的默认目标）、``pen``（当前正在数位板或屏幕上使用的笔），或 "
"``dial``。无法在指定目标上播放时，终端丢弃请求。"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:37
msgid "Discovery"
msgstr "能力探测"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:39
msgid "A program asks what the terminal can play::"
msgstr "程序查询终端可播放哪些反馈：::"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:43
msgid ""
"``id`` is a non-negative 31 bit integer of the program's choosing, echoed in the reply so replies"
" can be matched to queries. A supporting terminal answers::"
msgstr "``id`` 是程序自行选择的非负 31 位整数，回复原样返回，以便匹配查询。支持协议的终端回答：::"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:48
msgid ""
"``caps`` is a bit set. ``1``, ``2`` and ``4`` mean that taps can be played on the trackpad, on a "
"pen and on a dial: right now, on this machine, and the user has not turned them off. ``8`` means "
"that continuous feedback, described below, can be played on a pen. A terminal that does not "
"support the protocol ignores the query, so a program must time out. The answer can change, when a"
" pen is paired or the user changes a setting, so a program that was told a bit is clear may ask "
"again later."
msgstr ""
"``caps`` 为位集合。``1``、``2`` 和 ``4`` 分别表示当前机器此刻可在触控板、笔和旋钮上播放轻触，且用户没有关闭。``8`` "
"表示可在笔上播放下述连续反馈。不支持协议的终端会忽略查询，因此程序必须设置超时。配对笔或用户修改设置时，答案可能变化；曾得知某个位未设置的程序可稍后重试查询。"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:57
msgid "Taps"
msgstr "轻触反馈"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:64
msgid "``pattern`` is required and is one of:"
msgstr "``pattern`` 必需，取以下值之一："

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:67 docs/haptic-protocol.rst:120 docs/haptic-protocol.rst:123
#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:124
msgid "``generic``"
msgstr "``generic``"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:67
msgid "A single tap, for a drop or a touch"
msgstr "单次轻触，用于放下物体或接触"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:68 docs/haptic-protocol.rst:121
msgid "``alignment``"
msgstr "``alignment``"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:68
msgid "The tap used when a dragged object snaps into place"
msgstr "拖动物体吸附到位时的轻触"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:69 docs/haptic-protocol.rst:122
msgid "``level``"
msgstr "``level``"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:69
msgid "The tap used when a pressure sensitive control changes level"
msgstr "压力感应控件切换档位时的轻触"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:70 docs/haptic-protocol.rst:123
msgid "``click``"
msgstr "``click``"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:70
msgid "The tap of a button being pressed or a dial passing a detent"
msgstr "按钮按下或旋钮经过卡点时的轻触"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:71 docs/haptic-protocol.rst:124
msgid "``complete``"
msgstr "``complete``"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:71
msgid "The tap that says an action finished: a stroke was recognized as a shape, a path was closed"
msgstr "表示操作完成的轻触，例如笔迹识别成形状或路径闭合"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:75
msgid ""
"A terminal plays taps only for the focused window and at most once every 50 milliseconds per OS "
"window, and silently drops the rest. There is no reply."
msgstr "终端仅为获得焦点的窗口播放轻触，每个操作系统窗口最多每 50 毫秒一次，其余静默丢弃。不产生回复。"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:79
msgid "Continuous feedback"
msgstr "连续反馈"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:81
msgid ""
"A pen with a motor can make the glass feel like paper for as long as it draws. A program starts "
"that when a stroke begins and stops it when the stroke ends::"
msgstr "带马达的笔可在绘画期间让玻璃表面产生纸面质感。程序在笔划开始时开启，结束时关闭：::"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:88
msgid ""
"``pattern`` is required for ``start`` and names the tool whose feel is wanted: ``ink``, "
"``pencil``, ``marker``, ``brush`` or ``eraser``. ``intensity`` is a percent of full strength, "
"``0`` to ``100``, and ``100`` when absent. A ``start`` while feedback is playing on that target "
"replaces the pattern and the intensity, which is how a program follows the pressure of the pen. "
"``stop`` ends it; without a ``target`` it ends the continuous feedback on every target. Neither "
"has a reply, and the limit on how often taps are played does not apply to them."
msgstr ""
"``start`` 必须带 ``pattern``，指定所需工具质感：``ink``、``pencil``、``marker``、``brush`` 或 "
"``eraser``。``intensity`` 为最大强度的百分比，范围 ``0`` 至 ``100``，省略时为 ``100``。目标已播放反馈时，再次 ``start`` "
"会替换模式和强度，使反馈可跟随笔压力变化。``stop`` 结束反馈；未指定 ``target`` 时，停止所有目标上的连续反馈。两者均无回复，也不受轻触反馈频率限制。"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:97
msgid ""
"Continuous feedback must not outlive the program that asked for it, so a terminal stops it by "
"itself:"
msgstr "连续反馈不能在请求程序退出后持续，因此终端会在以下情况自行停止："

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:100
msgid "when the window loses focus,"
msgstr "窗口失去焦点；"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:101
msgid ""
"when one second passes without another ``start`` for that target, so a program that wants it to "
"go on repeats its ``start`` at least twice a second; a repeat with the same values is not felt,"
msgstr "某目标在一秒内未再次收到 ``start``。因此希望反馈持续的程序至少每秒重复两次 ``start``；相同值的重复不会产生可感知变化；"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:104
msgid "when the terminal is reset."
msgstr "终端被重置。"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:106
msgid ""
"A relay or a multiplexer forwards these requests for the pane that has the focus and does not "
"repeat ``start`` on a program's behalf."
msgstr "中继或多路复用器为获得焦点的窗格转发请求，不代替程序重复 ``start``。"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:110
msgid "Equivalents"
msgstr "各系统的对应模式"

#: docs/haptic-protocol.rst:112
msgid ""
"The patterns are those the systems with such hardware already offer, under the nearest name each "
"has. The first column of systems is the only one Silkie plays; the others are for terminals on "
"those systems."
msgstr "这些模式使用各硬件系统原有的反馈，采用最接近的名称。系统列中只有第一列由 Silkie 实际播放；其他列供相应系统上的终端实现参考。"

